    "text": "White light is passed through a double slit and interference is observed on a screen <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> away. The separation between the slits is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mm</mi></math>. The first violet and red fringes are formed <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mm</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mm</mi></math> away from the central white fringes. The difference in wavelengths of red and violet light is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mtext>in</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>nm</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>.</mo></math>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "300",
  "solution": {
